.\" sball-node-verify manual page
.TH SBALL-NODE-VERIFY 8 "2026-10-14" "sball-addition 1.0.0" "System Administration"
.SH NAME
sball-node-verify \- acceptance check for one PVM node running sball-addition
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B sball-node-verify
[\fB\-\-smoke\fR] [\fB\-\-json\fR] [\fB\-\-quiet\fR]
[\fB\-\-root=\fIdir\fR] [\fB\-\-prefix=\fIdir\fR]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B sball-node-verify
answers the question that matters before restarting a production node: is this
host really wired up, and will the hooks run? It inspects the installation and
exits non-zero when something that matters is broken, which makes it usable as
a gate in a rollout (see
.BR sball-rollout (8))
or in configuration management.
.PP
Checks performed:
.TP
\(bu
the
.B sball-addition
binary runs and reports its version
.TP
\(bu
the wrapper is installed and looks like
.BR sballd-wrapper
.TP
\(bu
the optional
.I /usr/sbin/sballd
shim and the real daemon
.RI ( /usr/sbin/sballd.real )
.TP
\(bu
the configuration file and
.B sball-addition validate
.TP
\(bu
the number of hooks per phase and their headers, ordering and executability
.TP
\(bu
hook and configuration permissions: a group or world writable hook is a
failure, because hooks execute as root
.TP
\(bu
systemd wiring: the
.I sballd.service
drop-in, the watcher unit and whether it is enabled and active
.TP
\(bu
a running watcher process (unit or wrapper spawned)
.TP
\(bu
writability of the state, runtime and log directories, and the last log record
.TP
\(bu
the PVM socket and the quorate state
.TP
\(bu
what the pre-quorate phase would run
.RB ( "sball-addition run-phase pre-quorate \-\-dry-run" )
.TP
\(bu
with
.BR \-\-smoke ,
a real round trip: a temporary post-quorate hook is installed, executed and
removed again
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.B \-\-smoke
Install, run and remove a temporary hook named
.IR zz-verify-smoke .
Proves that the runner, state directories and log are functional.
.TP
.B \-\-json
Print one JSON object
.RB ( ok ", " warnings ", " failures ", " healthy ", " checks )
instead of the human readable report.
.TP
.B \-\-quiet
Only print warnings, failures and the summary.
.TP
.BI \-\-root= dir
Installation root to check (default
.B $SBALL_ADDITION_ROOT
or
.IR / ).
.TP
.BI \-\-prefix= dir
Prefix of the program paths (default: the root).
.SH EXIT STATUS
.TP
.B 0
healthy (warnings are allowed, for example a missing shim or a socket that is
unreachable because the service is intentionally down)
.TP
.B 1
at least one check failed: do not restart this node yet
.TP
.B 2
usage error
.SH EXAMPLES
Check the local node and allow a temporary hook to run:
.PP
.RS
sball-node-verify \-\-smoke
.RE
.PP
Feed the result into a rollout or a CI job:
.PP
.RS
sball-node-verify \-\-json | jq \-e .healthy
.RE
.PP
Check an installation inside a test root:
.PP
.RS
sball-node-verify \-\-root=/tmp/stage
.RE
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR sball-addition (8),
.BR sball-rollout (8),
.BR sballd-wrapper (8),
.BR systemctl (1)
